1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,292
Two weeks ago, this project built something that runs two AI agents

2
00:00:03,292 --> 00:00:06,000
on the same company and flags when their numbers disagree.

3
00:00:06,708 --> 00:00:09,125
Last week, both agents finally became real.

4
00:00:09,542 --> 00:00:12,333
This week, it ran for the first time. And the first thing

5
00:00:12,333 --> 00:00:15,167
it produced wasn't a disagreement. It was a number that came from

6
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:15,967
nowhere.

7
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,550
The second agent ran on a model set up locally.

8
00:00:19,008 --> 00:00:20,883
Once it ran: real filing data went in.

9
00:00:21,383 --> 00:00:24,217
A real independent model came back with a conclusion for each side.

10
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:27,800
Producer A, reading assets, revenue, and net income, wrote: 'Calculated the

11
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:31,467
debt-to-equity ratio as zero point three four.' Its input data contained no

12
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:35,092
debt and no equity figures. Not close, not derived, the concept wasn't

13
00:00:35,092 --> 00:00:35,892
in the data at all.

14
00:00:36,258 --> 00:00:38,133
Producer B, reading real earnings figures,

15
00:00:38,842 --> 00:00:42,925
cited zero numbers. It described them, 'consistent,' 'significantly large,' but

16
00:00:42,925 --> 00:00:44,008
never wrote one down.

17
00:00:44,383 --> 00:00:46,133
The system flagged a contradiction.

18
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:48,800
It was right to. But not for the reason you'd hope.

19
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,117
One surprising result could be noise.

20
00:00:51,617 --> 00:00:54,700
So five separate tests ran against it, not a quick pass or

21
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,200
fail on each, but the full treatment:

22
00:00:56,617 --> 00:00:58,950
what the test is, why it was run, what a clean result

23
00:00:58,950 --> 00:01:02,033
should look like, exactly what was fed into it, what actually came

24
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:03,117
back, and what that means.

25
00:01:03,658 --> 00:01:04,492
Here's all five.

26
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:09,053
Five tests. One upstream extraction gap, one informative outlier,

27
00:01:09,428 --> 00:01:11,803
one mechanism that worked exactly as designed,

28
00:01:12,262 --> 00:01:14,595
one clean structural pass, and one real,

29
00:01:15,178 --> 00:01:17,595
project-redirecting flaw in what the flag actually measures.

30
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,693
The fix wasn't just tested against hand-built examples.

31
00:01:21,110 --> 00:01:24,818
It was checked against the same twelve real companies, recalculated, not re-run.

32
00:01:25,318 --> 00:01:27,693
Under the old rule: eleven of twelve flagged. Under the new rule:

33
00:01:27,818 --> 00:01:31,360
seven of twelve. Four companies, where one agent simply hadn't quantified anything,

34
00:01:31,527 --> 00:01:32,568
stopped being false alarms.

35
00:01:33,068 --> 00:01:35,985
The other seven, where both agents cited real numbers about different things,

36
00:01:35,985 --> 00:01:39,527
are still flagged. That's the honest, measured size of the fix. Not

37
00:01:39,527 --> 00:01:40,327
everything.

38
00:01:40,735 --> 00:01:42,652
Something specific and countable.

39
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,257
Two separate questions, two separate answers.

40
00:01:45,715 --> 00:01:49,340
Does the machinery work? Real filings, real independent reasoning, a full audit

41
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:52,298
trail, a guardrail that held on every one of twenty-four real calls.

42
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,340
Yes. Provably, not just theoretically.

43
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:58,632
Does the flag reliably mean these two agents disagree? Not yet. Most

44
00:01:58,632 --> 00:02:01,840
of what it flags right now is agents discussing different things, not

45
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,340
agents contradicting each other.

46
00:02:03,923 --> 00:02:07,340
And the one real fabrication this system produced was caught by a

47
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:08,548
person reading the output,

48
00:02:08,965 --> 00:02:10,215
not by the system itself.

49
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:15,070
A system built specifically to distrust fluent, confident answers just produced one,

50
00:02:15,362 --> 00:02:18,070
and then measured exactly how wrong it was, instead of hiding it.

51
00:02:18,403 --> 00:02:19,528
That's not a finished detector.

52
00:02:19,945 --> 00:02:22,528
It's a detector that's now told on itself, twice, in two days,

53
00:02:22,528 --> 00:02:25,362
once about a number, once about what its own flag actually measures.

54
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:28,570
The smallest true claim, not the biggest: this proved the plumbing.

55
00:02:28,945 --> 00:02:30,237
It did not yet prove the judgment.

56
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:34,055
That's the short version. The full video also covers Fast version.

57
00:02:34,513 --> 00:02:37,597
Cross-Agent Validation runs…, Test one: claim verification.

58
00:02:38,013 --> 00:02:41,472
Here's… and Test two: determinism. What it… — watch The Number That

59
00:02:41,472 --> 00:02:44,305
Wasn't There for the whole story. The link is right below.
